t":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279128044,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkxMjgwNDQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/confirmed","name":"confirmed","color":"aaddaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-03-14T13:42:08Z","updated_at":"2026-07-31T12:26:12Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Found in v4.6.1.stable.official [14d19694e]\n- Reproduced in v4.1.3.stable.official [f06b6836a]\nI have not tested it with other versions.\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Godot v4.6.1.stable.official [14d19694e]\n\n### Issue description\n\nDefining a dictionary like this in a script:\n```\nvar dictionary = {\n\t\t\"foo\": \"bar\"\n\t}\n```\nIs valid syntax, despite the overindented body and closing brace. It causes no errors or warnings, the script functions just fine, and the dictionary can be used normally.\n\nHowever, if you try to use the signals dock to connect a signal to one of the functions currently in the script, the editor will attempt to add a new function with the same name, which makes the script invalid.\n\nIt is possible to delete the added function. However, if the connection binds extra arguments, the signal connection will fail altogether, displaying an error like this:\n`ERROR: Cannot connect to 'pressed': the provided callable is not valid: 'Control::button_pressed'.`\nmaking it impossible altogether to connect certain signals in a scene without editing the scene file manually or fixing the indentation mistake.\n\nWhile I do not know if the dictionary definition above should be valid syntax or not, the fact that it doesn't cause any errors or warnings other than this one made it really hard to track down why the signal couldn't connect properly.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a new scene\n- Attach a script to the root node of the scene\n- Add this code to the script (note the overindented body and closing brace in the dictionary):\n```\nvar dictionary = {\n\t\t\"foo\": \"bar\"\n\t}\n\nfunc button_pressed():\n\tprint(\"pressed!\")\n```\n- Save the script and scene.\n- Go to the signals dock and try to connect any signal, from this node or a new one, to the `button_pressed` function.\n- When you click \"Connect\", a new function with the same name will be added to the script, making it invalid.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[TestSignalIssue.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25996067/TestSignalIssue.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117416/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117416/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}